### What
Adds support for the Payment Element using practices established in `StripeCardElement` . 

### Why
The Payment Element is an Element supports multiple payment methods. Adding support gives `vue-stripe` support for 18+ payment methods, including digital wallets.

### Usage
The `StripePaymentElement` takes in two required props: 

1. `elementOptions`, an object that specifies the [`PaymentIntent` client secret](https://stripe.com/docs/api/payment_intents/object#payment_intent_object-client_secret) (required). You can optionally specify the fonts, locale, and appearance. Learn more about these option properties in the [official Stripe docs](https://stripe.com/docs/js/elements_object/create#stripe_elements-options).
2. `confirmParams` an object that specifies the payment's `confirmParams` (required). You can learn more about optional confParams properties in [the official Stripe docs](https://stripe.com/docs/js/payment_intents/confirm_payment#confirm_payment_intent-options-confirmParams).  

```
<template>
  <div id="app">
    <stripe-payment-element
      v-if="argsReady"
      ref="elementRef"
      :pk="pk"
      :elementsOptions="elementsOptions"
      :confirmParams="confirmParams"
    />
    <button @click="submit">Pay</button>
  </div>
</template>

<script>
import { StripePaymentElement } from "@vue-stripe/vue-stripe";
import axios from "axios";

export default {
  name: "App",
  components: {
    StripePaymentElement,
  },
  data() {
    return {
      argsReady: false,
      pk: null,
      elementsOptions: {},
      confirmParams: {},
      backendUrl: process.env.VUE_APP_BACKEND_URL,
    };
  },
  async created() {
    this.confirmParams = {
      return_url: "http://localhost:8080/",
    };

    axios
      .all([
        axios.get(`${this.backendUrl}config`),
        axios.get(`${this.backendUrl}payment-intent`),
      ])
      .then(
        axios.spread((pk, paymentIntent) => {
          this.pk = pk.data.publishableKey;
          this.elementsOptions = {
            clientSecret: paymentIntent.data.clientSecret,
            appearance: { theme: "night" }, // optional theme
          };
          this.argsReady = true;
        })
      );
  },
  methods: {
    submit() {
      this.$refs.elementRef.submit();
    },
  },
};
</script>

```

In addition, the `StripePaymentElement` also supports the follow optional props: 

| Prop  | Type | Description  |
| ----- | ----- | ------------ |
| [`createOptions`](https://stripe.com/docs/js/elements_object/create_payment_element#payment_element_create-options) | object | Options for creating the Payment Element |
| [`redirect`](https://stripe.com/docs/js/payment_intents/confirm_payment#confirm_payment_intent-options-redirect)  |  string | Specifies whether the Payment element should for redirect only when required the payment method requires it  |
| [`stripeAccount`](https://stripe.com/docs/js/initializing#init_stripe_js-options-stripeAccount) |  string | Sets the Stripe account when using Stripe Standard Connect |
| [`apiVersion`](https://stripe.com/docs/js/initializing#init_stripe_js-options-apiVersion)   |  string | Sets the API Version  |
| [`locale`](https://stripe.com/docs/js/initializing#init_stripe_js-options-apiVersion)  |  string | Sets the locale on the Stripe object |

